<title>USA: Liberty Tech to sell unit to GE.</title>
<headline>Liberty Tech to sell unit to GE.</headline>
<dateline>CONSHOHOCKEN, Pa. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Liberty Technologies Inc said Friday it had agreed to sell its nondestructive evaluation and testing services business to a subsidiary of General Electric Co for $13.6 million cash plus the assumption of certain operating liabilities.</p>
<p>The purchase price is subject to reduction based on the balance sheet at closing, and 10 percent of the purchase price will be held in escrow to secure the company's indemnification liabilities.</p>
<p>Liberty said it expects to consummate the transaction by October 31.</p>
</text>
